  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Find the integers $a$ and $b$ in each equation.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2-\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}}=a-4\\sqrt{b}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=7,\\ b=3$",
          "worked": "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $2-\\sqrt{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{2-\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}} &= \\frac{(2-\\sqrt{3})^2}{4-3} \\\\\n\\frac{2-\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}} &= \\frac{4-4\\sqrt{3}+3}{1} \\\\\n\\frac{2-\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}} &= 7-4\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing with $a-4\\sqrt{b}$ gives $a=7$ and $b=3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}=a-\\sqrt{b}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=4,\\ b=15$",
          "worked": "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}} &= \\frac{(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3})^2}{5-3} \\\\\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}} &= \\frac{5-2\\sqrt{15}+3}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}} &= 4-\\sqrt{15}\n\\end{align*}$$\n\nComparing with $a-\\sqrt{b}$ gives $a=4$ and $b=15$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
  },
